  "details": "I believe that the new Social/Friends List looks bad.\n\nI say this because, removing the ability to look at the Avatar Details in the menu is flawed since Uses can gatekeep public avatars and most users that ask, don't know that they can look at avatar details in the sub/small menu.\n\nNameplates, I'd say this is also a downgrade as they can make the represented group look squashed or cropped too much.\n\nAlso in the most recent update, Inviting a User after they crash is now bugged as you cannot invite them as the game registers them as if they're online causing a Pop Up bellow the menu stating \"Unable to invite user. User is currently offline\".\n\nThe new Profile User Interface looks far too \"website like\" which I personally dislike as I didn't mind how it looked pre update; that and due to this change,  Bios have be expanded. Furthermore, The \"Avatar Details\" button on the profile menu is no where to be found, and clicking onto the instance in which a friend is in is now impossible.\n\nSo I propose that you could revert some of the UI changes so that the UI doesn't look as squashed and to also Aid users to find the avatar details page more easily.\n\n \n\n- Docttore",
